WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.112
Who is this for?

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:02.500
Developers build it.

3
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.400
Identity engineers run the waves
and keep the conversion file.

4
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.770
And the application owners
switch each workload,

5
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.975
keep the cutover log, and
approve every disable.

6
00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:14.787
The access is split in two.

7
00:00:14.787 --> 00:00:19.024
The read path is an app with read-only
permissions and the Reader role.

8
00:00:19.024 --> 00:00:22.985
The write path is only ever a person,
signed in with their own roles,

9
00:00:22.985 --> 00:00:26.797
because a standing app with the
right to add credentials to any

10
00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:30.537
application is exactly what this
program is trying to remove.

11
00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:32.366
For the identity's credential,

12
00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:36.000
the code picks the narrower
built-in role over Contributor.
